# Local-only active context (working-memory-kit)
_working-memory/activeContext.md

# The auto-sync commits anything untracked, Python bytecode included.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The normalizers replace their encrypted source by renaming a temp file into place, and
# that temp has to sit in the source dir for os.replace to stay atomic. A SIGKILL between
# the two steps strands it here. Each script sweeps stale ones on its next write, but the
# daily sync's `git add -A` may run first, so this is what keeps one out of a commit.
.normalize-tmp-*

# The sync's capture writes dot_config/macos-defaults.captured through a temp beside it; a killed
# run strands one, and `git add -A` in the daily sync would commit it.
dot_config/macos-defaults.captured.*

# tests/mutation-check.sh rewrites a test file by renaming a sidecar into
# place, and only SIGKILL can now strand one. The daily sync's `git add -A`
# must not commit it.
tests/*.mutated
